# Lint before commit

Before creating a git commit (or opening/updating a PR with code changes), always run local static analysis and fix failures:

```bash
npm run lint
```

That runs Terraform fmt/TFLint/validate, `astro check`, and API `node --check` (same gates as `.github/workflows/ci-static-analysis.yml`).

## Rules

- Do not commit or push changes that fail `npm run lint`.
- If you only touched infra, you may run `npm run lint:terraform` first, but still run the full `npm run lint` before the commit when feasible.
- If a required tool is missing (`terraform`, `tflint`), install it or tell the user — do not skip the gate silently.
- CI job names to keep green on PRs: Terraform lint, Site check, API syntax, Actions secret-safety. When `infra/` changes, Plan staging / Plan prod run only after those succeed. After merge, `CD: terraform` applies. Do not `terraform apply` locally unless the user explicitly asks — see `no-local-deploy.mdc`.
- When changing `.github/workflows/**`, also check for Node.js 20 action runtimes and upgrade them — see `github-actions-node.mdc`. Run `npm run lint:actions-secrets`.
- Never echo secrets — see `never-echo-secrets.mdc`.
- When the PR implements a planned phase, update `docs/plans/*` — see `plans-status-on-pr.mdc`.
- When the PR changes a store, schema, relation, or access path, update `docs/architecture/data-persistence.md` — see `data-persistence.mdc`.
